JOC: write the clip gain as DEE does (joc_clipgain_x_bits 4).

The encoder wrote joc_clipgain_x_bits 0 with y 0, which this project's
decoder reads as unity. tvOS 27.0 applies 2^(x-4) to the reconstructed
objects, so an Apple TV played every object at exactly 1/16 (-24 dB). DEE
always writes x=4, y=0, which is unity under either reading; with it, tvOS's
object levels match this project's own decode within 0.2 dB. Not part of the
seal. Updates the header test, adds a round-trip check, and notes the
observation where the decoder's clip-gain reading is documented. Apply after
05-signing-docs.

---

